Microbait: A lightweight, stupidly simple honeypot

DESCRIPTION
Microbait is a lightweight honeypot that logs any
connection data from connections instantiated by 
outside users using tools like Netcat.

CONFIGURATION
Microbait can be configured with its configuration file, named 'microbait.conf'.
Here, you can alter the values of the fields to fit your needs:

1. port: the port number that Microbait will be listening for connections on. It is 
highly recommended to use an unused port to avoid port collisions, which may 
cause service accessibility issues on your system.

2. service: the name of the service or service banner that will be sent over
to the connected user after he or she instantiates a connection on the designated 
port.

3. max-bytes: the total number of bytes that should be received from the connecting user
in order to prevent an overload of unnecessary connection data. It is recommended to keep
this value as a power of 2 and not too high. by default, the maximum bytes that Microbait
will receive from connecting user is 64 KiB.

GENERAL USE
In the directory you have downloaded Microbait in, run the command: “python3 microbait.py”. 
Ensure that microbait.conf is in the same directory as the script is.
Microbait will automatically start listening on the port you assigned it to
listen on in its configuration file. It will continue to listen on this port as long
as its maximum bytes to be received has not been equalled or exceeded, or as long as
the user deploying it has not stopped or terminated it. When a connecting user
has been detected, Microbait will inform you in the terminal it was launched in and 
begin logging data it send over if it decides to do so. Additionally, Microbait will
take note of the source IP address, the source port, and the time the connection was made.
Once Microbait is finished, it will generate a structured JSON file detailing the connections
along with the relevant data mentioned in the last sentence.

